{title: 288 - I Am Going to Calvary}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #288 • SEE SAW SACCARA DOWN • 7.7.7.8.7.7.7.7}
{lyricist: Brian Wren}
{composer: Charles Strange}
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 288}
{meta: tune SEE SAW SACCARA DOWN}
{meta: meter 7.7.7.8.7.7.7.7}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]I am going to [Gm]Calvary,
[Bb]Would you [Cm]like [Bb7/Ab]to come [Fm]with Me
[Eb]All the way and back again?
[Bb]You must [Cm]follow [Bb7]the Leader [Eb]then.
[Eb/G]You must follow [Ab]the [Fm]Leader,
[Eb]You must follow the Leader,
[Eb]All the way [Bb7]and back [Cm]again,
[Bb7]You must follow [Fm]the Leader.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]If I wear a [Gm]thorny crown,
[Bb]If the [Cm]soldiers [Bb7]knock [Fm]Me down
[Eb]Can I really be a [Bb]king?
[Bb]Love will [Cm]answer [Bb7]everything
[Eb/G]If you follow [Ab]the [Fm]Leader,
[Eb]If you follow the Leader,
[Eb]Love will answer [Bb7]everything
[Bb7]If you follow [Fm]the Leader.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]When I go along [Gm]the road,
[Bb]I shall [Cm]lift [Bb7/Ab]a heavy [Fm]load.
[Eb]I will carry a cross for [Bb]you.
[Bb]You will [Cm]learn [Bb7/Ab]to carry [Fm]it [Eb]too
[Eb/G]When you follow [Ab]the [Fm]Leader,
[Eb]When you follow the Leader,
[Eb]You will learn to [Bb7]carry [Cm]it [Bb7/Ab]too
[Bb7]If you follow [Fm]the Leader.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Eb]I am going to [Gm]stretch My hands,
[Bb]Reaching [Cm]out [Bb7/Ab]to all [Fm]the lands.
[Eb]Can I really be a [Bb]king?
[Bb]Love's [Cm]the [Bb7/Ab]Lord of everything,
[Eb/G]When you follow [Ab]the [Fm]Leader,
[Eb]When you follow the Leader,
[Eb]Love's the Lord [Bb7]of everything
[Bb7]When you follow [Fm]the Leader.
{end_of_verse}
